-- title:
--   Answer Family Point Consistency Error Eq Avg
-- statement:
--   **Successor point consistency decomposes as the uniform average of slice consistency errors.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $\widehat S$ be an answer-valued symmetric strategy for $(m+1,q,d)$, and let $G^x$ be an indexed family of polynomial submeasurements for the base parameters $(m,q,d)$. The bipartite consistency error between the successor point measurement and the family evaluated at points $(u,x)\in\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}$ is exactly the uniform average over the slice height $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$ of the consistency error between the point measurement of the restricted answer-valued strategy at height $x$ and the pointwise evaluation of $G^x$:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{ConsErr}^{\mathrm{bi}}_{\psi,\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1})}
--   \bigl(A_{\mathrm{pt}}(\widehat S),\operatorname{EvalNext}(G^x)\bigr)
--   =\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}
--   \left[
--   \operatorname{ConsErr}^{\mathrm{bi}}_{\psi,\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^m)}
--   \bigl(A_{\mathrm{pt}}(\widehat S_x),\operatorname{Eval}(G^x)\bigr)
--   \right].
--   $$
--
--   Here $\widehat S_x$ is the restricted answer-valued strategy at height $x$. The identity is used by `answer_family_consistency_of_slice_bounds`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MainInductionStep.answer_family_pointConsistencyError_eq_avg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
